    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`). \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `namesakeCount` on `POST /api/owners` \u2014 the number of existing owners (before this create) sharing the same firstName and lastName, compared case-insensitively.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `namesakeCount` (int32, min 0) property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field and MapStruct maps it by name.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `namesake_count` column mapped to an `Integer namesakeCount` field with getter/setter.\n\n3. **`schema.sql`** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `namesake_count` column to the `owners` table.\n\n4. **`AssignNamesakeCount.java`** \u2014 a new OfficeFloor function that reads the built `@Val Owner`, counts existing owners whose first and last names match case-insensitively via `equalsIgnoreCase`, and sets the count on the owner. It runs before `SaveOwner`, so the new owner is not counted.\n\n5. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted the `assignNamesakeCount` step (under `transaction` governance) between `assignHousehold` and `save`.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreCountsNamesakes` (two owners sharing `Ann <last>`, expecting `namesakeCount == 1` on the second) passes, as does the full suite.",
